    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6c3b
    pr_ref:  # 6c3b
    description: "WHAT (measured 2026-11-19). scripts/test-leaderboard _parse_junit_xml turns junit's classname into a path by treating its last dotted part as a test class. For a method of a class that is right (packages.hypergumbo-core.tests.test_x.TestK -> packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_x.py::TestK::name). For a module-level test function the last part is the MODULE, so packages.hypergumbo-core.tests.test_x -> packages/hypergumbo-core/tests.py::test_x::name, and tests.test_y -> tests.py::test_y::name. In ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/test_timings.json: 10,755 package keys and 1,892 root keys in that form (12,647 of 41,671, 30%); NO module-level function is stored under its correct id; corrected, all 12,647 are unique and every file exists (not collisions, not duplicates). EFFECT: every join of timings to test ids misses them, e.g. smart-test's 'estimated wall time' (matches key files against the selection) counts them as 0 s. FIX: when the last dotted part of classname is a module (it names a test_*.py / BRANCHES_test_*.py file, or does not start with an upper-case letter... decide by checking the file), build path::name; rewrite the stored keys once (merging runs if a correct key exists). CLOSE CONDITION: a test with a module-level function's junit row; the store holds 0 keys of the broken form after one ingest + the one-off rewrite."  # 6c3b
    fields: {}  # 6c3b
